%N A398941 Decimal expansion of the midradius of a canonical (dual-uniform) 10-gonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398941 The 10-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 10-gonal antiprism.
%H A398941 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398941/b398941.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398941 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Decagonal_antitegum">Decagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398941 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398941 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_08">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 8</a>.
%F A398941 Equals csc(Pi/20)*sqrt(1 + 2*cos(Pi/10))/4 = csc(Pi/20)*sqrt(1 + A188593)/4.
%F A398941 Equals the largest real root of 256*x^8 - 2048*x^6 + 1104*x^4 + 88*x^2 + 1.
%e A398941 2.722480194684437494559933334759410555785465685143...
%t A398941 First[RealDigits[Csc[Pi/20]*Sqrt[1 + 2*Cos[Pi/10]]/4, 10, 100]]
%t A398941 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398941 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 10}, "Midradius"], 10, 100]]
%Y A398941 Cf. A398938 (volume), A398939 (surface area), A398940 (inradius), A398942 (height).
%Y A398941 Cf. A398943 (long edge).
%Y A398941 Cf. A398944 (small face angle), A398945 (large face angle), A398946 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398941 Cf. A395806 (midradius of the dual).
%Y A398941 Cf. A188593.
